            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Hersheykissed"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Very Good! I didnt have a graham cracker crust just a regular deep dish frozen pie crust. I baked the empty 9 inch deep dish pie crust and filled it once it was completly cooled. Everyone enjoyed. I had the pie before with coconut in it but didnt have any on hand. I added 2 tsp of coconut rum cream liquer, and it gave it just the right amount of coconut essence without the coconut. I followed the directions as written, however I only used 8oz of whip cream, and as the pic shows i had a full pie.",
            "datePublished": "2010-12-28T17:34:18.020Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "iguanamama"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Such an easy pie. I made this for my sorority meeting and none came home with me. I put toasted coconut that I had mixed with green food coloring and made a tree on top with cherries as ornaments. Will for sure make again and again.",
            "datePublished": "2023-12-06T02:52:52.097Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "daniellewinsted"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I love this pie!! Had never heard of it til a couple years ago. However my husband used to have this for thanksgiving as a kid. It was this same recipe only we added coconut and chopped maraschino cherries! It’s a great addition to this amazing pie!! If you haven’t tried it. You have to!",
            "datePublished": "2018-11-23T04:39:07.863Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "snuggles6891"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This is a great recipe but I made one change (which I believe I heard another reviewer mentioned)which was adding 8oz Philadelphia Cream Cheese to the Whipped Cream. I also found that you can replace the crushed pineapples with other fruits. For instance, using thawed frozen strawberries instead of crushed pineapples. This was a winner. Note: I wouldn't suggest mixing both crushed pineapples and frozen strawberries unless you like a very tangy pie.",
            "datePublished": "2012-08-26T09:04:31.433Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Diana Chistruga"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I loved the crunch from the graham cracker crust and pecans-it balanced perfectly with the creaminess of the filling. The sweetness was just right, with the pineapple adding a hint of tartness. A little tip: if you want to make slicing easier, chill the pie overnight.",
            "datePublished": "2024-11-22T11:43:11.429Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "TNGwife"
            },
            "reviewBody": "We have made this pie for years in our family. It actually calls for one 9\" crust, but I have always divided it into two crusts. I usually keep one and take one to work. It is so simple to make. This one also says ready in 2 hrs, but we have always made the night before. My cousin actually adds cream cheese and mandrin oranges. This a very good recipe especially during the hot summer months.",
            "datePublished": "2009-02-16T11:52:12.383Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "rose175"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This is a great recipe! You only need 8 oz of whipped topping. I used only 8 oz and my pie was overflowing in the crust! I think using 16 oz would definitely be too much. This is a very good recipe- light and airy but full of great flavor! Good fix for the sweet tooth!",
            "datePublished": "2012-12-23T21:21:14.250Z"
          },
